Lanternfall: credits and licences

Code: this repository (MIT, see LICENSE). Every texture, sprite, sound and piece of music is generated by code in this
repository; no third-party art or audio is shipped, so there is nothing further to attribute.

Where each asset comes from
- assets/world.bin: the world generator (src/worldgen.c, run by tools/worldgen.c). assets/route.bin: the checker
  (tools/check.c).
- Tile sets, normal maps, ledges, thorns, back walls, parallax silhouettes, glows: generated at start-up by src/art.c.
- The hero, enemies, wardens, props, lamps and effects: drawn from shapes every frame by src/view.c.
- Sound effects and music: synthesised at start-up by src/audio.c.
- Launcher art (art/): the game's own frames, cropped and composited with ImageMagick; the logo is text set in
  DejaVu Sans Bold (Bitstream Vera licence, free to use and embed) by ImageMagick.
